# Backend Security

## Must keep
- Gateway: Helmet, allowlisted CORS, class-validator whitelist/forbidNonWhitelisted, JWT + roles + permissions guards
- Passwords: bcrypt (prefer 12 rounds); lockout + Turnstile + optional TOTP where already implemented
- Tokens: separate RSA keypairs for access/refresh; rotate refresh via session delete; never log secrets/JWTs/PII
- Webhooks: verify provider signatures before mutating state
- Payments: never trust client amounts; verify Razorpay server-side

## Hard rules for new code
- Never commit secrets, private keys, or password-bearing URLs. Prefer Infisical → `.env.infisical` (runtime only)
- Never accept client `x-user-id` / `x-user-role` as identity on public routes — gateway must overwrite from JWT only
- Prefer bearer auth; if cookies are used, pair with CSRF and SameSite discipline
- Do not weaken WS auth (issuer/audience/type checks, algorithm allowlist). Avoid `origin: '*'` + credentials
- Rate-limit auth, contact, media upload, and payment initiation paths
- Metrics/admin/debug ports must not be world-exposed without auth
- Redact query strings and secrets in logs (`redact-url` helpers)

## When reviewing changes
Call out missing authz on new endpoints, IDOR (resource ownership checks), unsigned webhooks, plaintext secrets, and unauthenticated admin/impersonation paths.
